vdo.dev.write_amplification PMID: 129.5.182 [Ratio of backing-store writes to incoming write bios]
    Data Type: float  InDom: 129.5 0x20400005
    Semantics: instant  Units: none
Help:
Ratio of physical (data plus metadata) write bios issued by VDO to its backing
store per incoming write bio, i.e. (bios.out + bios.meta) / bios.in for writes.
A value above 1 indicates write amplification from metadata and journalling.
Only available via the device-mapper stats message backend (in-tree dm-vdo,
kernel 6.9 and later); no value is returned on the legacy /sys/kvdo backend.
No value(s) available!

vdo.dev.emulation_512 PMID: 129.5.183 [Whether the VDO emulates a 512-byte logical block size]
    Data Type: 32-bit unsigned int  InDom: 129.5 0x20400005
    Semantics: discrete  Units: none
Help:
Set to 1 when the VDO presents a 512-byte logical block size (emulation) rather
than the native 4KiB, otherwise 0.  Only available via the device-mapper stats
message backend (in-tree dm-vdo, kernel 6.9 and later); no value is returned on
the legacy /sys/kvdo backend.
No value(s) available!

